# Employee Referral Bonus Scheme

> Module ReferralBonus

## Prologue — declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ReferralBonus:
  input grade content integer
  input is_hard_to_fill content boolean
  input agency_introduced content boolean
  input agency_introduction_date content date
  input referral_date content date
  input first_day_of_employment content date
  input has_ceased content boolean
  input cessation_date content date
  input cessation_by_redundancy content boolean
  input bonus_already_paid_this_year content money
  internal agency_introduction_is_stale content boolean
  internal ceased_within_qualifying_period content boolean
  output qualifying_period_end content date
  output entitlement content money
  output payable content boolean
  output bonus_before_cap content money
  output bonus_payable content money
```

## B-2 Definitions

| REF-BONUS B-2.2 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:23)
|
| "Qualifying Period" means the period of 180 days beginning on the Referred
| Hire's first day of employment.

The period begins ON the first day, so the first day is day 1 and the period
runs to the 179th day after it.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  definition qualifying_period_end equals
    first_day_of_employment + 179 day
```

## B-3 Bonus entitlement

| REF-BONUS B-3.1 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:31)
|
| An Employee who makes a referral resulting in a Referred Hire is entitled to
| a bonus of £1,000.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label b3_1 definition entitlement equals $1,000.00
```

| REF-BONUS B-3.2 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:34)
|
| By way of exception to B-3.1, where the Referred Hire is engaged at Grade 5
| or above, the bonus is £2,500.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label b3_2 exception b3_1 definition entitlement
    under condition grade >= 5
    consequence equals $2,500.00
```

| REF-BONUS B-3.3 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:37)
|
| By way of exception to B-3.1 and B-3.2, where the role is a Hard-to-Fill
| Role, the bonus is £4,000.

B-3.3 is an exception to both earlier limbs, so it sits below B-3.2 in the
chain and thereby defeats B-3.1 as well.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label b3_3 exception b3_2 definition entitlement
    under condition is_hard_to_fill
    consequence equals $4,000.00
```

| REF-BONUS B-3.4 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:41)
|
| Notwithstanding B-3.3, no bonus is payable where the candidate was
| introduced to the Company by a recruitment agency before the referral was
| submitted.

"Notwithstanding B-3.3" places this below the highest limb of B-3, so it
defeats the whole of B-3.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label b3_4 exception b3_3 definition entitlement
    under condition
      agency_introduced and agency_introduction_date < referral_date
    consequence equals $0.00
```

| REF-BONUS B-3.5 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:45)
|
| By way of exception to B-3.4, where the agency introduction occurred more
| than 12 months before the referral was submitted, the bonus is payable and
| is calculated under B-3.1 to B-3.3.

The condition of B-3.4 is repeated here, because a Catala exception does not
inherit its parent's condition. The consequence re-derives the B-3.1 to B-3.3
result rather than naming a figure, since B-3.5 restores that calculation
rather than fixing an amount of its own.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  definition agency_introduction_is_stale equals
    agency_introduction_date + 12 month < referral_date

  label b3_5 exception b3_4 definition entitlement
    under condition
      agency_introduced
      and agency_introduction_date < referral_date
      and agency_introduction_is_stale
    consequence equals
      if is_hard_to_fill then $4,000.00
      else if grade >= 5 then $2,500.00
      else $1,000.00
```

## B-4 Payment and forfeiture

| REF-BONUS B-4.2 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:52)
|
| No bonus is payable where the Referred Hire ceases employment before the
| expiry of the Qualifying Period.

| REF-BONUS B-4.3 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:55)
|
| By way of exception to B-4.2, where the Referred Hire ceases employment by
| reason of redundancy, the bonus remains payable.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  definition ceased_within_qualifying_period equals
    has_ceased and cessation_date <= qualifying_period_end

  label b4_base definition payable equals true

  label b4_2 exception b4_base definition payable
    under condition ceased_within_qualifying_period
    consequence equals false

  label b4_3 exception b4_2 definition payable
    under condition
      ceased_within_qualifying_period and cessation_by_redundancy
    consequence equals true
```

| NO-CLAUSE: combining the B-3 entitlement with the B-4 payability test adds no
| law of its own; both are stated above. It exists so that the B-5 cap has a
| single quantity to apply to, as B-5.2 requires.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  definition bonus_before_cap equals
    if payable then entitlement else $0.00
```

## B-5 Aggregate limit

| REF-BONUS B-5.1 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:60)
|
| The total bonus payable to an Employee under this Scheme in any financial
| year must not exceed £10,000.

| REF-BONUS B-5.2 (referral-bonus-scheme.md:63)
|
| The limit in B-5.1 is applied after any adjustment under B-3 and B-4.

The cap is on the TOTAL for the year, so the amount available for this
referral is the limit less what has already been paid, and never below nil.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  definition bonus_payable equals
    let headroom equals $10,000.00 - bonus_already_paid_this_year in
    if headroom <= $0.00 then $0.00
    else if bonus_before_cap > headroom then headroom
    else bonus_before_cap
```
